Asset type: three-direction art comparison for Twyne, an editorial writing instrument, NOT a finished website or UI mockup.
Primary request: Create ONE wide transparent contact sheet containing THREE well separated small illustrations of the SAME subject in THREE distinct, sophisticated editorial styles. The subject is a sentence-revision bench: two narrow off-white paper wording slips laid next to one another, a short red editorial pencil, and a small dark metal composing stick. The objects must be legible at a thumbnail size. Use meaningful short hatch strokes for writing instead of words.
Left vignette: 'Copperplate tools' direction, precise mid-century book engraving, confident warm-black etched contour lines and exquisite controlled hatching, little red pencil accent, opaque pale paper slips, clean readable outer silhouette.
Center vignette: 'Letterpress cutouts' direction, bold, flat cut-paper and linocut silhouettes, muted indigo-black shapes and a single red editing accent, deliberately tactile broken ink edges, strongest thumbnail legibility.
Right vignette: 'Paper theatre' direction, a crafted miniature paper diorama, precise folded cardstock, clean architectural shape, soft bounded contact shadows, same cream / warm black / red palette, slightly raised paper slips and pencil.
Composition: three separate vignettes on one row, aligned optical height, 25 percent empty space between them, objects take up central 60 percent of their area. Use an approximately 3:1 wide canvas. Each is independent, no overlapping the other vignette.
Palette: warm-black #1f1b16, ivory #faf3df, small vermilion #c1272d. Dark indigo #2c4a7c permitted in center only.
